          "body": "Argentina's coach Álvaro Galindo has named a 27-man Argentina XV to play England A in Bath in an uncapped match, with Benetton hooker Bernardo Bernasconi, who has three caps, heading the squad. The match gives players from both sides a chance at call-ups to the test arena. The squad includes Harlequins prop Pedro Delgado, Bristol Bears flanker Benjamín Grondona and Clermont fly-half Juan Segundo Martín Montilla, who is 19. The squad trained for four days at Hindú Club in Buenos Aires."
